    "Amprenavir L2 records conflict between very high and almost zero, leaving that context noisy."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high because the closest transferable context, KNI-272, has absolute oral bioavailability of 22-55% for capsule formulations across doses and prandial states in patients, and the query shares the same hydroxyethylamine and tert-butyl amide scaffold. L2 records add two more KNI-272 capsule values above 20% and confirm darunavir absolute 37%, while low values appear only in syrup formulations or in species with poor transferability. The only clearly low-F context, alvimopan at 6%, is structurally unrelated. Confidence stays moderate because formulation sensitivity and structural differences leave residual uncertainty."
}

